26:37.560 --> 26:40.560
is that in a closed-loop control,

26:40.560 --> 26:43.560
we are constantly measuring the state,

26:43.560 --> 26:47.560
and our control action depends on the current value of the state.

26:48.560 --> 26:52.560
This is a bit subtle, so I want to make sure that every one of you

26:52.560 --> 26:54.560
appreciate this part.

26:54.560 --> 26:58.560
Our formulation is deterministic. There is no uncertainty.

26:58.560 --> 27:01.560
There are no random variables, nothing. Purely deterministic.

27:01.560 --> 27:07.560
So if you give me initial condition and a control function,

27:07.560 --> 27:09.560
I can tell you exactly where my system will be,

27:09.560 --> 27:11.560
say, 10 seconds from now.

27:12.560 --> 27:18.560
Which means that if I apply a function that is only a function of time

27:18.560 --> 27:22.560
and a function that is a function of time and state,

27:22.560 --> 27:27.560
since I will always be following my nominal trajectory,

27:27.560 --> 27:31.560
the two will not really give rise to any difference.

27:33.560 --> 27:37.560
So why would we might possibly be interested in closed-loop control?

27:38.560 --> 27:41.560
Again, let me be more specific here.

27:45.560 --> 27:50.560
Open-loop is only a function of time,

27:50.560 --> 27:54.560
so it tells me at each instant of time

27:54.560 --> 27:56.560
which control action I should follow.

27:56.560 --> 27:59.560
And let's say that this is the trajectory that I get,

27:59.560 --> 28:01.560
x open-loop, x off.

28:03.560 --> 28:05.560
This is an open-loop.

28:05.560 --> 28:09.560
Closed-loop is a function of both the state and time,

28:09.560 --> 28:14.560
which means that if I'm here at a given time t,

28:14.560 --> 28:16.560
I take an action,

28:16.560 --> 28:18.560
but if I'm a different state, say, here,

28:18.560 --> 28:20.560
I may take a different action.

28:20.560 --> 28:24.560
In open-loop, no matter where I am at the current time,

28:24.560 --> 28:26.560
I always take the same action.

28:27.560 --> 28:31.560
With closed-loop, at a given time, depending on where I am,

28:31.560 --> 28:33.560
I may take different actions.

28:34.560 --> 28:37.560
So why closed-loop is actually super useful?

28:37.560 --> 28:41.560
Closed-loop is useful is that all models are wrong

28:41.560 --> 28:43.560
