44:27.560 --> 44:30.560
on top of some input constraints,

44:30.560 --> 44:32.560
that is good enough is particularly simple.

44:32.560 --> 44:36.560
Simple means that you can compute it very fast.

44:36.560 --> 44:37.560
Well, you want to compute very fast.

44:37.560 --> 44:39.560
As an autonomous robot is moving around,

44:39.560 --> 44:42.560
the environment is changing around the robot,

44:42.560 --> 44:45.560
so often you have to recompute your trajectory.

44:45.560 --> 44:47.560
So it's imperative that you close the loop

44:47.560 --> 44:52.560
at usually at least about 1 hertz, possibly 10 hertz.

44:53.560 --> 44:57.560
So differential flatness is a very deep topic

44:57.560 --> 45:00.560
in mathematics and differential geometry.

45:00.560 --> 45:02.560
So here, I'm just going to give you

45:02.560 --> 45:05.560
the operational version of differential flatness.

45:05.560 --> 45:09.560
And to do so, let me start with a motivating example.

